<%# THE ACCOUNTS, DEMOTED TO ONE LINE (answers-first spec §6). Local: `presenter` (HomePresenter).

    ** WHAT THE LINE ANSWERS AND WHAT THE EXPANSION IS FOR, because they are two different jobs. **
    The line answers "how much of my money is somewhere other than checking" — main is deliberately
    out of the figure, because main's balance IS the hero's "In Checking" number and printing it
    again here would answer one question twice. The expansion is the accounts INDEX: Home carries
    rename and delete since `pools/index` and `pools/show` were deleted, so every finished account's
    card has to stay reachable, main's included.

    `<details>`/`<summary>` RATHER THAN A STIMULUS CONTROLLER — the house idiom, and
    `budget_page/_suggestions.html.erb` states its reason where the same choice was made: the whole
    interaction is "show me the rest", it needs no JavaScript, and it survives a Turbo navigation.
    The SUMMARY carries the figure, always visible, because the figure is the answer.

    ONBOARDING IS NOT IN HERE. An account still awaiting its funding card, and main still awaiting
    its opening balance, render top-level (see `index.html.erb`) — a door behind a chevron is a door
    a first-time user does not find. `HomePresenter#collapsed_accounts` is the one place that split
    is made, so the two lists cannot both claim an account and render its card twice. %>
<% accounts = presenter.collapsed_accounts %>
<% others = presenter.other_accounts %>
<% if accounts.any? %>
  <details class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded" data-accounts>
    <summary class="px-6 py-3 text-sm text-gray-700 cursor-pointer hover:text-gray-900" data-accounts-line>
      <% if others.any? %>
        <strong class="tabular-nums"><%= number_to_currency(presenter.other_accounts_total) %></strong>
        across <%= pluralize(others.size, "other account") %>
        <%# ** THE CHIPS ARE GONE FROM HERE (2026-09-06 layout ruling), AND THEY WENT UP RATHER THAN
            AWAY. ** They were added here because the line said how MUCH was elsewhere and never
            WHERE — and the money row's third tile now answers that at the top of the screen, in the
            first band, beside the figure it is about. Printing the same three names again at the
            foot of the page was the same list twice on one screen, which is the thing this whole
            wave is undoing. What this line keeps is its own job: the total, and the door to the
            cards behind it. `data-account-chip` on the tile is the one hook that names them. %>
      <% else %>
        <%# NOTHING IS ELSEWHERE, so there is no figure to state — "$0.00 across 0 other accounts"
            would be the app inventing an absence. The line still exists, because the cards behind it
            do and this is the only door to them.

            "ACCOUNT DETAILS", NOT "YOUR ACCOUNTS" (account-openings spec §3): that is the heading of
            the card below, and one screen saying the same three words twice about two different
            things reads as one thing rendered twice. This line is the door to the finished accounts'
            cards; the card below is where an account is added and where it says what it holds. %>
        Account details
      <% end %>
    </summary>

    <%# A TRAY RATHER THAN A CONTINUATION OF THE CARD: `_account` renders its own bordered section,
        so the expansion is given a recessed ground to sit them on instead of a second set of
        borders butted against this one. %>
    <div class="border-t border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-3 space-y-3">
      <%# TODAY'S ACCOUNT CARDS, UNCHANGED. `_account` is the same partial it was — the balance the
          bank says, the main-account note, rename and (off main) delete. %>
      <% accounts.each do |account| %>
        <%= render "account", presenter: presenter, account: account %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </details>
<% end %>
